    "title": "Check Whether a Binary Tree is Height Balanced",
    "category": "Trees",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "problemStatement": "Given the root of a binary tree, determine whether the tree is height balanced. A binary tree is height balanced if, for every node, the difference between the heights of its left and right subtrees is at most one.",
    "input": "\u2022 The first line contains an integer N. \u2022 The next N lines describe the binary tree.",
    "output": "\u2022 Print YES if the tree is height balanced; otherwise print NO.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 0 \u2264 N \u2264 2 \u00d7 10^5________________________________________"
